"Installing an operating system onto a USB drive can be a convenient way to "
"try Qubes. However, USB drives are typically much slower than internal SSDs. "
"We recommend a very fast USB 3.0 drive for decent performance. Please note "
"that a minimum storage of 32 GiB is required. If you want to install Qubes "
"OS onto a USB drive, just select the USB device as the target installation "
"device. Bear in mind that the installation process is likely to take longer "
"than it would on an internal storage device."
